#HSSS 1.0
TITLE: Ubuntu White Edition / cryptsetup Specification
PACKAGE: cryptsetup
LANGUAGE: C
STATUS: W2
ROLE: LUKS/dm-crypt encrypted storage management

## PROGRAM
cryptsetup manages encrypted block-device mappings and LUKS metadata through established Linux storage and cryptographic interfaces.

## STRUCTURE
SOURCE: upstream cryptsetup / Ubuntu package
BOUNDARY: user request -> metadata/key handling -> dm-crypt mapping -> block storage
WHITE_EDITION: recovery, diagnostics, configuration overlay
GUI: optional JavaFX administration with explicit confirmation and privileged backend

## SPEC
- preserve LUKS compatibility
- protect key material from diagnostics/logging
- explain recovery requirements
- avoid destructive ambiguity
- use established cryptographic implementations

## QUALITY
TEST: create/open/close, encrypted I/O, wrong key, metadata, recovery, upgrade
ECONOMY: startup, memory, encryption throughput

## SOURCE POLICY
Primarily C. Native changes require concrete security/correctness justification. Do not implement replacement cryptographic primitives.
